                <pb facs="0567" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg381"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Editor’s Note</hi></head>
                <p>—At a meeting of the United States and Soviet Chiefs of Staff on July 26, Army
                    General Antonov stated that Stalin had handed to Truman the Soviet answer to
                        <ref target="#d1279">document No. 1279</ref>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>, at 11 a.m. on July 25 (see <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>,
                        <ref target="#pg408">page 408</ref>). No other record of this transaction,
                    which presumably took place at the Cecilienhof Palace immediately before the
                    Ninth Plenary Meeting, has been found.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
